**Restatement of the Problem:**
We are given n houses, and m existing roads, forming a partially connected graph. Each house i has a cost a[i], and to build a new road between houses u and v costs a[u] + a[v]. The existing roads are free. We have to add roads to make the whole network connected at minimal total cost, and output the roads we propose to add.

**Solution Outline:**

- Use DSU to track connected components after building the initial graph with the input edges.
- For each component, find the house with the minimal price (cheapest house in the component).
- The key insight: To connect all components at minimal cost, connect the overall globally cheapest house to the cheapest house in each other component. Since each road costs sum of the prices, this "star" connection minimizes overall cost.
- The number of new roads is (number of components - 1), and for each, connect the global cheapest house to the cheapest house in a different component.

**C++ Solution:**

```cpp
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;

struct DSU {
    vector<int> par;
    DSU(int n) : par(n+1) {
        iota(par.begin(), par.end(), 0);
    }
    int find(int x) {
        if (par[x] != x) par[x] = find(par[x]);
        return par[x];
    }
    void unite(int x, int y) {
        par[find(x)] = find(y);
    }
};

int main() {
    ios::sync_with_stdio(0);
    cin.tie(0);
    int n, m;
    cin >> n >> m;
    vector<long long> a(n+1);
    for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i)
        cin >> a[i];
    DSU dsu(n);
    for (int i = 0; i < m; ++i) {
        int u, v; cin >> u >> v;
        dsu.unite(u, v);
    }
    // Find cheapest in each component
    map<int, pair<long long, int>> cmp_min;
    for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {
        int root = dsu.find(i);
        if (cmp_min.count(root) == 0 || cmp_min[root].first > a[i])
            cmp_min[root] = {a[i], i};
    }
    if (cmp_min.size() == 1) {
        cout << "0\n";
        return 0;
    }
    // Find the overall minimal
    long long minv = LLONG_MAX; int minNode = -1, minRoot = -1;
    for (auto &x : cmp_min) {
        if (x.second.first < minv) {
            minv = x.second.first;
            minNode = x.second.second;
            minRoot = x.first;
        }
    }
    vector<pair<int,int>> roads;
    for (auto &x : cmp_min) {
        if (x.first == minRoot) continue;
        roads.push_back({minNode, x.second.second});
    }
    cout << roads.size() << endl;
    for (auto &r : roads) cout << r.first << ' ' << r.second << '\n';
}
```

**Explanation:**
- Use DSU to find connected components after incorporating the initial roads.
- For each component, find the representative node with the minimal price.
- Find the global minimal price node.
- For each component except that one, add a road (and track it).
- Output number of new roads and the roads themselves.

