The user asks for a C implementation of the extended Euclidean algorithm (Thuật toán Euclide mở rộng) exactly following the iterative pseudocode steps provided.

Here's a proper implementation and explanation:

```c
#include <stdio.h>

int extendedEuclid(int a, int b, int *x, int *y) {
    int x2 = 1, x1 = 0;
    int y2 = 0, y1 = 1;
    int q, r, x_temp, y_temp;

    while (b > 0) {
        q = a / b;
        r = a - q * b;
        x_temp = x2 - q * x1;
        y_temp = y2 - q * y1;

        a = b;
        b = r;
        x2 = x1;
        x1 = x_temp;
        y2 = y1;
        y1 = y_temp;
    }
    *x = x2;
    *y = y2;
    return a;
}

int main() {
    int a, b, x, y, d;
    printf("Nhap a: ");
    scanf("%d", &a);
    printf("Nhap b: ");
    scanf("%d", &b);

    d = extendedEuclid(a, b, &x, &y);
    printf("GCD(%d, %d) = %d\n", a, b, d);
    printf("He so x = %d, y = %d\n", x, y);
    printf("Kiem tra: %d*%d + %d*%d = %d\n", a, x, b, y, a*x + b*y);
    return 0;
}
```

**Explanation:**  
- Correctly follows the algorithm: initializes x2, x1, y2, y1; iteratively updates them in the loop based on the quotient and remainder.
- Returns d, x, y corresponding to the equation \( a \cdot x + b \cdot y = \gcd(a, b) \).

