**My Solution:**

**Restatement:**  
Given a sorted set of integer points on a line, can we add an integer not already in the set such that this new point becomes the closest point to every point in the set?

**Analysis:**  
For each original point x, its closest neighbor is at a distance d(x):  
- for the ends, d(x) is the only neighbor difference  
- for middle points, d(x) is the minimum of the two neighbors.

The new point p should satisfy, for every xi:  
|p - xi| < d(xi) ∀ xi  
i.e., the new point is strictly closer to xi than any other existing point.

But the problem statement says "there is no other point from the set such that the distance... is strictly less than the distance from j to i"; that is, the new point must be one of the closest points, i.e., tied if distances are equal.

Let's check what's possible:

- For each xi, let d(xi) be its minimal existing distance.
- For p to be closest to xi, |p - xi| ≤ d(xi).
- But since p ≠ xi (must not be the same as existing point), we must check for an integer p ≠ xi such that |p - xi| ≤ d(xi) for all xi.

So, for each xi, the allowed range for p is [xi - d(xi), xi + d(xi)], p ≠ xi.

Take the intersection of all such intervals, and check if there's an integer in the intersection not among the set itself.

**Implementation outline (C++):**
- For each test case, read n and the sorted points.
- For each point, compute d(xi) as described.
- For each xi, compute its feasible interval.
- Find the intersection [L, R] of all intervals.
- For each integer in [L, R], if it's not in the given set, output YES.
- Otherwise, output NO.

**C++ Code:**
```cpp
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;
int main() {
    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);
    cin.tie(0);

    int t; cin >> t;
    while (t--) {
        int n; cin >> n;
        vector<int> pts(n);
        for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) cin >> pts[i];

        vector<int> mindist(n);
        for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {
            if (i == 0) mindist[i] = pts[1] - pts[0];
            else if (i == n-1) mindist[i] = pts[n-1] - pts[n-2];
            else mindist[i] = min(pts[i] - pts[i-1], pts[i+1] - pts[i]);
        }
        int L = INT_MIN, R = INT_MAX;
        for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {
            L = max(L, pts[i] - mindist[i]);
            R = min(R, pts[i] + mindist[i]);
        }
        set<int> pts_set(pts.begin(), pts.end());
        bool found = false;
        for (int p = L; p <= R; ++p) {
            if (!pts_set.count(p)) {
                found = true;
                break;
            }
        }
        cout << (found ? "YES" : "NO") << '\n';
    }
}
```

